E["item:grimtotem-satchel"] = {t="item",n="Grimtotem Satchel",z="ragefire",s="Deep beneath Orgrimmar, Grimtotem Satchel remains in Maur Grimtotem’s grasp. Troggs killed the tauren in Ragefire Chasm, but he shielded the pouch as he died. Its return to Thunder Bluff brings Magatha Grimtotem’s interest to light.",h="Deep beneath Orgrimmar, Grimtotem Satchel remains in Maur Grimtotem’s grasp.",sec={{t="A Dying Grip",b="Maur Grimtotem fell to troggs deep inside Ragefire Chasm, beneath Orgrimmar. The tauren still clutched the simple leather pack when his body was found. He had fought to protect it while the troggs surrounded him. What could it hold that made him guard it with his life?",sp=0},{t="The Elder Crone's Interest",b="Rahauro on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff accepts the satchel for Magatha Grimtotem, matriarch of the Grimtotem clan. Maur served Magatha, and word had reached her that he found something peculiar in the caverns beneath Orgrimmar before he died. She arranged a reward for the pack’s safe return. The Grimtotem leader had a clear interest in what Maur found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Grimtotem Satchel found?",a="The Grimtotem Satchel was found beneath Maur Grimtotem’s body, deep inside Ragefire Chasm, the volcanic cavern beneath Orgrimmar. His arms still held it where troggs killed him.",al={"satchel location","where is the satchel","how to find satchel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does the satchel belong to?",a="The satchel belonged to Maur Grimtotem, a member of the Grimtotem clan who entered Ragefire Chasm. He held it close as troggs attacked.",al={"who owns the satchel","maur satchel owner"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the satchel returned?",a="Rahauro on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff accepts the satchel for Magatha Grimtotem. Magatha arranged a reward for the return of her fallen clansman’s belongings.",al={"who gets the satchel","who turns in satchel","who wants grimtotem satchel"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was a Grimtotem carrying this under Orgrimmar?",a="Maur Grimtotem served Magatha Grimtotem, who took an interest in Ragefire Chasm. He went there to speak with the troggs and found something peculiar, but died before he could show it to her.",al={"why was maur in ragefire","what was the grimtotem doing in orgrimmar"},it="motive"},{q="What is inside the satchel?",a="The pouch’s contents remain sealed when Rahauro receives it in Thunder Bluff. Magatha hopes it holds signs of the peculiar thing Maur found in the chasm.",al={"satchel contents","what is in the bag"},it="item"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="A Grimtotem went deep beneath Orgrimmar, then word of what he found reached Magatha on the Elder Rise. The clan’s moves within the united tauren tribes are quiet and uneasy.",["faction:Horde"]="A dead Grimtotem courier lay deep in the tunnels beneath Thrall’s capital. Ragefire Chasm holds dangers beyond its beasts."},kw={"elder rise","grimtotem","magatha grimtotem","maur grimtotem","ragefire chasm","rahauro","satchel","thunder bluff","trogg"},rel={"quest:5724","npc:maur-grimtotem","npc:rahauro","zone:ragefire","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:elder-rise","topic:tauren","topic:trogg"},src={"Grimtotem Satchel","Returning the Lost Satchel"}}
E["item:incantations-from-the-nether"] = {t="item",n="Incantations from the Nether",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Searing Blade cultists hold Incantations from the Nether, a grimoire of demonic magic. Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras seek its fel knowledge for the Forsaken.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Searing Blade cultists hold Incantations from the Nether, a grimoire of demonic magic.",sec={{t="Gifts of the Legion",b="The Searing Blade is a subterranean sect tied to the Shadow Council, working in the fiery tunnels of Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar's red stone streets. Its cultists prize Incantations from the Nether, a spellbook of demonic rites given by agents of the Burning Legion. They use its secrets to plot treason in the Orcish capital. Word of the tome has reached the royal quarters of Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Ambition",b="Varimathras sends loyal Horde adventurers deep into Ragefire Chasm to recover Incantations from the Nether and its sister volume, Spells of Shadow. Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant see such fel relics as wasted on cultists with lesser vision. The Dark Lady means to wield the book's nether-forged power against the Lich King and bring retribution to the Scourge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the book Incantations from the Nether found?",a="Searing Blade cultists and warlocks carry the book in Ragefire Chasm, the volcanic cavern network beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"where to get incantations from the nether","who drops incantations from the nether","incantations from the nether location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this book and why?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the dreadlord Varimathras seek the book. They consider the Searing Blade cultists petty, with lesser vision, and want its demonic magic to fight their sworn enemy, the Lich King.",al={"who needs incantations from the nether","why does sylvanas want this book","varimathras book quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Searing Blade?",a="The Searing Blade is a secretive subterranean sect of warlocks and cultists beneath Orgrimmar, allied with the Shadow Council. Its members serve the Burning Legion and work in secret to undermine Thrall's new Horde.",al={"searing blade lore","who are the searing blade"}},{q="What other book is paired with this one?",a="Varimathras requires two volumes: Incantations from the Nether and Spells of Shadow. Both must be taken from the cultists in Ragefire Chasm to complete his mission.",al={"other book for varimathras","power to destroy books"},it="item"},{q="What is Incantations from the Nether?",a="Incantations from the Nether is a dark grimoire containing fel spellcraft gifted by the Burning Legion. It came into the possession of the Searing Blade, a hidden cult of the Shadow Council operating deep within the fiery chasms beneath Orgrimmar. Alongside its sister tome, Spells of Shadow, the book holds potent demonic rituals that cultist warlocks study to harness the powers of the Twisting Nether.",al={"what is incantations from the nether","incantations from the nether book","what kind of book is incantations from the nether"},it="identity",add="e0d58fa2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Recovering the book aids the Dark Lady's inner circle in Undercity. The dark knowledge is needed to wage war against the Scourge.",["class:Warlock"]="Tomes drawn directly from the Nether hold potent fel magic, coveted by ambitious practitioners of the dark arts."},kw={"incantations from the nether","ragefire chasm","searing blade","shadow council","spells of shadow","sylvanas","the power to destroy","varimathras"},rel={"quest:5725","item:spells-of-shadow","npc:varimathras","zone:ragefire","topic:forsaken","topic:shadow-council","zone:undercity","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Incantations from the Nether","The Power to Destroy... (Classic)"}}
E["item:spells-of-shadow"] = {t="item",n="Spells of Shadow",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Spells of Shadow rests in the hands of Searing Blade cultists. The Forsaken leadership in the Undercity wants the grimoire recovered.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Spells of Shadow rests in the hands of Searing Blade cultists.",sec={{t="Tomes of the Searing Blade",b="Searing Blade cultists keep Spells of Shadow among their guarded treasures in Ragefire Chasm. The splinter cult is tied to the Shadow Council, and its members wield dark rites granted by demon masters of the Burning Legion. The book holds shadow and fel sorcery. Cultists and warlocks keep it close as they plot beneath the Horde in Durotar.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Lady's Ambition",b="Word of the Searing Blade's demonic gifts reached the Undercity's royal quarters. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras, decided the relics were wasted on cultists with lesser vision. Varimathras sends Horde adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to seize Spells of Shadow and its companion tome, Incantations from the Nether. Their power is meant to serve the Forsaken cause against the Scourge and the Lich King.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Spells of Shadow?",a="Spells of Shadow is a spellbook held by the Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm. It contains shadow magic granted by the Burning Legion.",al={"spells of shadow book","what is spells of shadow","shadow spells book rfc"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants this book?",a="Varimathras seeks the tome for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. He is her dreadlord advisor and resides in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"who needs spells of shadow","who turns in spells of shadow","spells of shadow quest giver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the book be found?",a="Searing Blade cultists and warlocks carry the book in Ragefire Chasm, fiery caverns beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"spells of shadow location","where to get spells of shadow","how to get spells of shadow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want this grimoire?",a="Lady Sylvanas believes the Legion's dark gifts belong in Forsaken hands rather than with lesser cultists. She wants the magic to strengthen the Forsaken against the Scourge and the Lich King.",al={"why does sylvanas want the book","why does varimathras want spells of shadow"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you help Lady Sylvanas claim dangerous demonic knowledge beneath Orgrimmar and strengthen the Undercity against the Scourge.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see how Searing Blade cultists wield shadow and nether arts through demonic gifts from the Legion."},kw={"incantations from the nether","ragefire chasm","searing blade","spells of shadow","sylvanas","the power to destroy","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:5725","item:incantations-from-the-nether","zone:ragefire","npc:varimathras","zone:undercity","topic:shadow-council","topic:forsaken","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Spells of Shadow","The Power to Destroy... (Classic)"}}
E["item:taragaman-the-hungerer-s-heart"] = {t="item",n="Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade seeks Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart as proof the demonic presence has been purged. The grisly trophy comes from the felguard who rules Ragefire Chasm's depths.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade seeks Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart as proof the demonic presence has...",sec={{t="A Trophy of Deceit",b="Taragaman the Hungerer's steaming heart is proof that the felguard has fallen. Neeru Fireblade tells Thrall and eager adventurers that Taragaman directs the Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm. Bringing the heart to Neeru appears to fulfill the Warchief's order to guard Orgrimmar from demonic corruption. Blaming a brutish felguard for leading the cult also keeps the mortal networks beneath the city out of sight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart?",a="Neeru Fireblade, an orc warlock in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, asks you to bring him the heart as proof the demon has been slain.",al={"who takes taragaman heart","taragaman heart turn in","who wants the heart"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do I obtain this heart?",a="You take the heart from Taragaman the Hungerer's corpse in Ragefire Chasm's central magma chambers beneath Orgrimmar. The imposing felguard dwells there.",al={"how to get taragaman heart","where does taragaman heart drop","taragaman heart location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Does Thrall ever see the heart?",a="No. You bring the heart straight to Neeru Fireblade. He says he will handle the demonic remains and tell Warchief Thrall of the victory for you.",al={"does thrall get the heart","give heart to thrall","thrall taragaman heart"}},{q="Was Taragaman truly the leader of the Searing Blade?",a="Neeru Fireblade names Taragaman the Hungerer as the Searing Blade's leader and says slaying him and bringing back his heart will appease Thrall.",al={"is taragaman the leader","who leads searing blade","taragaman real boss"},sp=1},{q="What is Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart?",a="It is the severed heart of Taragaman the Hungerer, a massive felguard lurking in the fiery depths of Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. Carried out of the caverns by adventurers, it serves as physical proof that the demon Neeru Fireblade names as the Searing Blade's leader has been struck down.",al={"what is taragaman heart","taragaman the hungerer heart","taragaman heart lore"},it="identity",add="a71e3ad9"},{q="Where does Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart come from?",a="The heart is carved from the chest of Taragaman the Hungerer, an enormous felguard stationed deep within Ragefire Chasm. Taragaman was summoned and harbored in the subterranean tunnels beneath Orgrimmar by the Searing Blade cultists, making the heart an organic relic of the demonic corruption infesting the city's underbelly.",al={"taragaman heart origin","where did the heart come from","who made taragaman heart"},it="origin",add="d8388abb"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect Orgrimmar from corruption within. The beast's severed heart marks the Horde's vigilance.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know the delicate web of shadow and deception at play in the Cleft of Shadow. Dealing with Neeru Fireblade and handling demonic remains are familiar matters."},kw={"felguard","heart","hungerer","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","taragaman"},rel={"npc:taragaman-the-hungerer","quest:5761","quest:829","zone:ragefire","zone:orgrimmar","quest:5726","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart","Slaying the Beast (quest)"}}
E["npc:bazzalan"] = {t="npc",n="Bazzalan",z="ragefire",s="Bazzalan commands the Searing Blade cult from the lava caverns beneath Orgrimmar. Alongside Jergosh the Invoker, he directs its work in Ragefire Chasm.",h="Bazzalan commands the Searing Blade cult from the lava caverns beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Serpent Beneath the City",b="Beneath Orgrimmar, Bazzalan has joined the Searing Blade cult in Ragefire Chasm. While Thrall works to establish the Orcs' new home across Durotar, the satyr rogue commands the cult's field forces from winding lava caverns. He is swift and lethal with twin blades.",sp=0},{t="Cult Leadership and Deceit",b="From a volcanic ledge above the central chamber, Bazzalan oversees the cultist guards. Jergosh the Invoker conducts demonic rituals below. Like all satyrs, Bazzalan's ultimate loyalty belongs to demonic masters. He uses poison, quick strikes, and stealth against Horde scouts who venture near the cult's staging ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bazzalan?",a="Bazzalan is a satyr rogue who shares leadership of the Searing Blade cult inside Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"bazzalan lore","who is bazzalan","satyr boss rfc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Bazzalan be found in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Bazzalan lurks on the upper ledges of Ragefire Chasm, above Jergosh the Invoker. Dark ramps cut into the cavern walls lead up to him.",al={"bazzalan location","where is bazzalan","find bazzalan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a satyr doing beneath Orgrimmar?",a="Bazzalan works with the Searing Blade, a demonic cult seeking to undermine the Horde from within. Satyrs are bound to demonic powers and often serve as instigators and assassins for shadow councils.",al={"why is there a satyr in orgrimmar","why is bazzalan in rfc"},it="why_here"},{q="What abilities does Bazzalan use in combat?",a="Bazzalan attacks swiftly with melee weapons and uses Sinister Strike. He sometimes afflicts opponents with a mild debilitating poison.",al={"bazzalan abilities","bazzalan attacks","how does bazzalan fight"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is his relationship to Jergosh the Invoker?",a="Bazzalan and Jergosh share leadership of the Searing Blade inside Ragefire Chasm. Jergosh handles invocations and summoning dark forces, while Bazzalan commands the cult's martial and stealth work.",al={"jergosh and bazzalan","is bazzalan related to jergosh"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the Horde want Bazzalan dead?",a="Bazzalan's presence deep beneath the capital is a direct demonic threat. Horde leaders send adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to eliminate him before the Searing Blade's plot endangers the city.",al={"bazzalan bounty","repel the invasion bazzalan"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Bazzalan on?",a="Bazzalan serves the demonic masters behind the Shadow Council. Operating directly alongside Jergosh the Invoker, he commands the Searing Blade cultists lurking beneath Orgrimmar, working in secret against the Horde and the safety of the city above.",al={"who does bazzalan serve","bazzalan faction","bazzalan allegiance"},it="side",add="9fcb4f3a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Bazzalan and his cult pose a hazard beneath Thrall's stronghold, and the Horde wants them eliminated.",["class:Rogue"]="Bazzalan uses stealth, vicious strikes, and venom-coated blades, making him an opponent of particular interest to Rogues.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs fought hard to escape demonic manipulation. A satyr directing cultists in their own foundations is an outrage to them."},kw={"bazzalan","cultist","jergosh","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rfc","satyr","searing blade"},rel={"zone:ragefire","npc:jergosh-the-invoker","topic:satyr"},src={"Bazzalan"}}
E["npc:jergosh-the-invoker"] = {t="npc",n="Jergosh the Invoker",z="ragefire",s="Deep beneath Orgrimmar, Jergosh the Invoker plots against the Horde. He leads Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm and practices demonic arts while Thrall guides the orcs toward honor and shamanism.",h="Deep beneath Orgrimmar, Jergosh the Invoker plots against the Horde.",sec={{t="A Cult Beneath the City",b="Jergosh gathers the Searing Blade beneath Orgrimmar. While Thrall leads the orcs toward honor and shamanism, Jergosh turns to demonic power. He hides in Ragefire Chasm, where he draws followers into a sect aligned with the remnants of the Shadow Council. From below the Horde capital, the cult works against the path the new Horde has chosen.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Ambitions",b="Jergosh's work in Ragefire Chasm draws Thrall's direct scrutiny. Dark rituals and dangerous schemes have grown bold enough to attract the Warchief's attention. Within Durotar, Jergosh keeps alive the dark pacts the Horde fought to leave behind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jergosh the Invoker?",a="Jergosh the Invoker leads the Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm. He rejects Thrall's honorable path and embraces demonic sorcery.",al={"who is jergosh","jergosh lore","jergosh ragefire"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Jergosh hiding in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Jergosh hides in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, where the Searing Blade can practice dark magic and conspire against the Horde.",al={"why is jergosh under orgrimmar","jergosh location lore"},it="why_here"},{q="What faction does Jergosh belong to?",a="Jergosh leads the Searing Blade, a cult linked to the Shadow Council and devoted to demonic interests like the Burning Legion.",al={"jergosh faction","is jergosh shadow council","searing blade leader"},it="side"},{q="Does Thrall know Jergosh is beneath Orgrimmar?",a="Yes. Jergosh's plots grew dangerous enough to reach Thrall, who sent trusted adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to stop the cultists.",al={"thrall jergosh","does thrall know about ragefire"}},{q="Why does Jergosh practice fel magic instead of shamanism?",a="Jergosh rejects shamanistic harmony and turns to demonic sorcery, seeking the power of the Burning Legion and the dark arts.",al={"why warlock","jergosh fel magic"}},{q="What does Jergosh the Invoker want?",a="Jergosh aims to undermine the Horde from within its own capital. Rejecting Thrall's renewed shamanistic ideals, he seeks to revive dark demonic practices and further the nefarious ambitions of the Shadow Council. Lurking in the chasm, he concocts subversive schemes dangerous enough to threaten the stability of Orgrimmar itself.",al={"jergosh goal","what does jergosh want","jergosh motive"},it="wants",add="3ff8bf73"},{q="Who is Jergosh the Invoker tied to?",a="Jergosh is a prominent leader among the Searing Blade cultists, a subterranean coven operating right beneath Orgrimmar. The cult is secretly an arm of the wider Shadow Council, binding Jergosh directly to the shadowy network of warlocks and demon worshipers seeking to pull the orcish people back into corruption.",al={"jergosh allies","who does jergosh work for","jergosh shadow council"},it="ties",add="752417a2"},{q="Why is Jergosh the Invoker feared?",a="Jergosh is feared because he wields forbidden fel magic right beneath the feet of the Horde's leadership. His dark rituals, demonic summoning, and radical rejection of the new Horde's path pose an existential internal threat, drawing the direct attention and concern of Warchief Thrall himself.",al={"why is jergosh feared","is jergosh dangerous","jergosh reputation"},it="fame",add="baae249b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see in Jergosh the old Horde's lingering pull toward demonic blood and sorcery, which Thrall seeks to purge from orcish culture.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face a powerful practitioner of the demonic arts whose schemes threaten the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="A Shadow Council cell beneath the chieftain's throne room is a security threat the Horde cannot ignore."},kw={"invoker","jergosh","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","shadow council","warlock"},rel={"zone:ragefire","topic:shadow-council","npc:thrall","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Jergosh the Invoker"}}
E["npc:maur-grimtotem"] = {t="npc",n="Maur Grimtotem",z="ragefire",s="Deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, Maur Grimtotem lies dead. Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem sent him to seek peace with the troggs, and his remains and satchel are still in the caverns.",h="Deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, Maur Grimtotem lies dead.",sec={{t="A Doomed Diplomacy",b="Maur Grimtotem went into Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar as an envoy to the troggs. Most of the Horde saw them as savage brutes beyond negotiation, but Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem thought peace might be possible, or at least said so. Maur carried her offer into the winding caverns. The troggs killed him, and his body remains under the watch of their chieftain, Oggleflint.",sp=0},{t="The Elder Crone's Interests",b="After Maur's death, Magatha sought adventurers to retrieve the satchel he carried into the caverns, as well as avenge him. Whether Maur believed peace with the troggs could be reached remains unknown. Those who find his belongings may still wonder whether Magatha sent him as a true envoy or as a pawn in her schemes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Maur Grimtotem?",a="Maur Grimtotem was a tauren of the Grimtotem clan. Magatha Grimtotem sent him as an emissary to the troggs in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, where they killed him.",al={"who is maur","maur grimtotem lore","what was maur doing"},it="identity"},{q="Why did he try to negotiate with troggs?",a="Elder Crone Magatha claimed she sent Maur to seek peace and test the strength of the subterranean foes. Whether she had another motive remains an open question.",al={"why make peace with troggs","trogg diplomacy","why talk to troggs"},it="why_here"},{q="Who killed Maur Grimtotem?",a="The troggs of Ragefire Chasm killed Maur. Their chieftain, Oggleflint, guarded his body.",al={"how did maur die","who killed him","maur death"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to his body and belongings?",a="Maur's body remains in Ragefire Chasm near Oggleflint. Rahauro in Thunder Bluff sends adventurers to recover Maur's lost satchel and bring it to him on the Elder Rise for Magatha Grimtotem.",al={"maur corpse","lost satchel","maur's satchel"}},{q="Whose side was Maur Grimtotem on?",a="Maur answered directly to Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem and served the interests of the Grimtotem clan. While the Grimtotem are technically counted among the Horde through their uneasy presence on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise, Maur's loyalties and secret mission belonged solely to his clan.",al={"maur grimtotem faction","who does maur grimtotem serve","maur grimtotem alliance horde"},it="side",add="c7d44e51"},{q="What did Maur Grimtotem want?",a="Maur sought to forge an alliance or peaceful accord with the troggs infesting the chasms beneath Orgrimmar. Following Magatha Grimtotem's instructions, he ventured into Ragefire Chasm hoping to negotiate with the creatures, unaware that their feral and violent nature made any diplomatic understanding impossible.",al={"what was maur grimtotem doing","maur grimtotem mission","maur grimtotem goal"},it="wants",add="565aa8ac"},{q="Who was Maur Grimtotem tied to?",a="Maur was an emissary sent by Magatha Grimtotem, the matriarch of the Grimtotem clan who currently resides on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. He carried out her private designs below Orgrimmar, keeping his mission separate from the standard Horde leadership.",al={"who sent maur grimtotem","maur grimtotem connections","maur grimtotem magatha"},it="ties",add="bfc0472b"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Grimtotem clan has an uneasy relationship with the other tribes in Thunder Bluff. Maur's fatal errand into the trogg tunnels deepens suspicion of Magatha's agenda.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the danger of a deadly cavern beneath Orgrimmar. Sending envoys alone to negotiate with troggs ended in disaster."},kw={"grimtotem","magatha","maur","oggleflint","orgrimmar","ragefire","satchel","trogg"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:oggleflint","zone:ragefire","quest:5722","quest:5724","quest:5723","topic:trogg","topic:tauren"},src={"Maur Grimtotem"}}
E["npc:oggleflint"] = {t="npc",n="Oggleflint",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Oggleflint leads the trogg tribe in Ragefire Chasm. His pack climbs from lava-filled tunnels toward the surface, where he commands them near the cavern entrance and threatens the Horde capital above.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Oggleflint leads the trogg tribe in Ragefire Chasm.",sec={{t="Chieftain of the Deep",b="Deep beneath Orgrimmar, Oggleflint and his troggs climbed from fiery tunnels into Ragefire Chasm. They carved a primitive domain among the molten rock and defend it with brutal force. Troggs have little advanced civilization, and Oggleflint rules his pack through sheer strength.",sp=0},{t="Death to Envoys",b="Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem sent diplomats into the chasm to make peace with the troggs. The troggs turned on them and killed them. Maur Grimtotem, one of the envoys, lies dead in the caverns under Oggleflint’s watch. Near the cavern entrance, the chieftain waits and strikes at outsiders who venture into the dark.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Beneath Orgrimmar",b="Oggleflint’s tribe lives directly beneath Thrall’s capital, a hazard the Horde cannot tolerate. The troggs creep closer to the surface, and their volatile nature threatens to carry them into the Drag and Cleft of Shadow if left undisturbed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Oggleflint?",a="Oggleflint is a powerful trogg chieftain who leads his pack in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"oggleflint","who is oggleflint","ragefire trogg boss"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Oggleflint be found?",a="Oggleflint waits in Ragefire Chasm’s upper caverns, near the entrance tunnel. His pack holds the tunnels nearest the surface.",al={"where is oggleflint","oggleflint location","find oggleflint"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the troggs in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Troggs naturally dwell deep underground in subterranean volcanic networks. Oggleflint’s pack has climbed from the lava-filled tunnels beneath Orgrimmar toward the surface.",al={"why are troggs under orgrimmar","ragefire trogg lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is Oggleflint hostile to the Horde?",a="Troggs are fiercely territorial and violent. As Oggleflint and his followers press toward the surface, they threaten the Horde tunnels and the city above.",al={"why kill oggleflint","why fight oggleflint"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Oggleflint's relationship with the Searing Blade?",a="Oggleflint’s troggs and the Searing Blade cultists share the chasm, but nothing makes them allies. The troggs hold the tunnels near the entrance, while the cultists work in the deeper chambers.",al={"searing blade and oggleflint","are troggs with the cult"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Oggleflint on?",a="Oggleflint fights purely for himself and his trogg brethren. He shares no allegiance with the Horde, the Alliance, or the Searing Blade cultists who also lurk in the chasm, and his troggs attack any Horde defenders who descend into the dark.",al={"oggleflint faction","oggleflint alliance or horde","who does oggleflint serve"},it="side",add="b435b0f8"},{q="What does Oggleflint want?",a="Oggleflint wants to hold his tunnels. His troggs have been pushing up from the lava-filled depths toward the surface, and they kill any outsider who comes into the chasm, even envoys sent to make peace.",al={"oggleflint goals","what troggs want ragefire","oggleflint purpose"},it="wants",add="e0483c37"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Beneath Thrall’s fortress, Oggleflint’s troggs pose a wild, unpredictable security risk in the heart of Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="As a young orc proving your mettle in the trial of arms, facing the chieftain beneath the Drag tests your martial discipline.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face a heavy brute who relies on raw muscle and primal rage, not armor or discipline."},kw={"oggleflint","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","trogg"},rel={"zone:ragefire","topic:trogg"},src={"Oggleflint"}}
E["npc:taragaman-the-hungerer"] = {t="npc",n="Taragaman the Hungerer",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Taragaman the Hungerer prowls the molten caverns of Ragefire Chasm. The Horde seeks to destroy the hulking felguard, feared as the demonic master behind the Searing Blade cult, and end the demonic taint beneath the city.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Taragaman the Hungerer prowls the molten caverns of Ragefire Chasm.",sec={{t="The Beast Below",b="Taragaman the Hungerer prowls among Ragefire Chasm's magma pools, threatening Orgrimmar below. Scouts and young warriors sent into the dark caverns see the demonic felguard as the Searing Blade cult's leader. With infernal strength, he bends the weak-willed and corrupts the passages beneath Thrall's fortress.",sp=0},{t="Lethal Decoy",b="Taragaman the Hungerer commands the cult's fear, but its true leaders are the satyr Bazzalan and the warlock Jergosh the Invoker. The schemers use the towering felguard as expendable bait, a monstrous distraction that draws Horde defenders into the searing volcanic depths, where they can be slaughtered.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of demon is Taragaman the Hungerer?",a="Taragaman is a felguard, a brutal demonic shock trooper of the Burning Legion. He uses heavy melee strikes and fiery magic against intruders in Ragefire Chasm's magma caverns.",al={"what race is taragaman","taragaman demon type","is taragaman a demon"},it="identity"},{q="Is Taragaman the Hungerer the leader of the Searing Blade cult?",a="Taragaman is widely believed to lead the Searing Blade. He is the most fearsome demonic power in Ragefire Chasm, and young Horde defenders are sent to slay him as the cult's master. The chasm may hold more secrets than a single felguard.",al={"who leads searing blade","is taragaman in charge","taragaman cult leader"},it="leader"},{q="Why does the Horde want Taragaman dead?",a="The Horde wants Taragaman dead because an active demonic presence festers beneath its capital. His infernal corruption threatens Orgrimmar from within, and killing him is vital to securing the cavern passages beneath the streets.",al={"why kill taragaman","slaying the beast quest lore","taragaman orgrimmar threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Taragaman be found?",a="Taragaman resides deep within Ragefire Chasm, in subterranean volcanic tunnels reached from the Cleft of Shadow inside Orgrimmar.",al={"taragaman location","where is taragaman","taragaman ragefire chasm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to Taragaman's heart?",a="Victorious adventurers carve out Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart as proof of the beast's death and to complete the work of clearing the demonic vanguard beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"taragaman heart","heart of taragaman","slaying the beast heart"},it="item"},{q="How does Taragaman fight in combat?",a="Taragaman attacks with crushing physical blows, a powerful uppercut that sends foes through the air, and occasional bursts of Fire Nova that scorch those nearby.",al={"taragaman abilities","taragaman boss fight","taragaman mechanics"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Taragaman the Hungerer on?",a="Taragaman is allied with the Searing Blade cultists lurking beneath Orgrimmar, threatening the Horde from within.",al={"taragaman faction","who does taragaman serve","is taragaman searing blade"},it="side",add="512c0cfb"},{q="Why is Taragaman the Hungerer in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Taragaman dwells within the fiery depths of Ragefire Chasm, spreading demonic corruption beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"why is taragaman here","what is taragaman doing in ragefire","why is taragaman in orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add="1dbae35b"},{q="Who is Taragaman the Hungerer tied to?",a="Taragaman is associated with the Searing Blade cult within Ragefire Chasm. Discovering who directs its schemes requires investigating the chasm.",al={"who does taragaman work with","taragaman allies","taragaman bazzalan"},it="ties",add="376a0125"},{q="Why is Taragaman the Hungerer feared?",a="Taragaman is feared as a towering demonic terror lurking directly beneath the Horde's capital. His demonic influence threatens to corrupt Orgrimmar's citizens, and his brutal physical might makes him infamous among young defenders sent into the chasm to eliminate him.",al={"why is taragaman famous","is taragaman dangerous","why fear taragaman"},it="fame",add="5af082b3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For young Horde warriors and spellcasters, slaying Taragaman beneath Orgrimmar is a proving ground and helps protect the capital from demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you practice dark arts in the Cleft of Shadow above, while a wild, hostile felguard like Taragaman threatens the secrecy and safety of your craft.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you must stand firm against Taragaman's crushing blows and avoid being tossed into the lava by his brutal uppercuts."},kw={"bazzalan","demon","felguard","hungerer","jergosh","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","taragaman"},rel={"quest:5761","zone:ragefire","npc:bazzalan","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},src={"Taragaman the Hungerer"}}
E["quest:5722"] = {t="quest",n="Searching for the Lost Satchel",z="ragefire",s="Rahauro sends you from Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise into Ragefire Chasm. Magatha Grimtotem seeks her lost emissary Maur and the unusual discovery he made among the troggs.",h="Rahauro sends you from Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise into Ragefire Chasm.",sec={{t="A Grimtotem Mission Beneath Orgrimmar",b="Magatha Grimtotem hears on Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise that her emissary, Maur Grimtotem, entered the cavern beneath Orgrimmar to study the troggs and try to parley with them. He never returned, and rumors say he found something unusual shortly before his death. While Warchief Thrall and his advisers focus on the Shadow Council presence in Ragefire Chasm, the Grimtotem clan follows its own interests.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Emissary",b="Rahauro, Magatha Grimtotem’s attendant, sends warriors into Ragefire Chasm on her behalf. Deep in the lava-filled tunnels, Maur’s battered body lies near the trogg encampments. Crude clubs and bare fists killed him, but the troggs left his belongings untouched. His satchel and whatever secrets he sought remain for Magatha’s agents to recover.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends adventurers on this quest?",a="Rahauro, Magatha Grimtotem’s attendant on Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise, sends you into Ragefire Chasm.",al={"quest giver","who starts searching for the lost satchel","where to get quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Maur Grimtotem?",a="Maur Grimtotem was Magatha’s emissary. He entered Ragefire Chasm to study the troggs and try to communicate with them, but they beat him to death in the cavern depths.",al={"maur grimtotem","who was maur","what happened to maur"},it="people"},{q="Why was Magatha Grimtotem interested in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Magatha was interested in the troggs beneath Orgrimmar and sent Maur to try to communicate with them. After he discovered something unusual among them, she wanted his discovery brought to her.",al={"magatha troggs","why magatha cares about ragefire","why send maur"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Maur Grimtotem's corpse located?",a="Maur’s body lies deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, near the trogg territories along the underground paths.",al={"find maur","maur grimtotem location","where is maurs body"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did the troggs loot Maur after killing him?",a="No. The troggs left Maur’s clothing and satchel beside his battered remains.",al={"trogg loot","was maur robbed"},it="history"},{q="What happens after locating Maur's body?",a="Finding Maur’s body leads to the next step, Returning the Lost Satchel. You take his satchel to Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff with his findings.",al={"follow up quest","next quest after lost satchel","what to do with satchel"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rahauro want Maur's satchel recovered?",a="Rahauro acts directly on behalf of Elder Magatha Grimtotem. Magatha learned that her servant Maur discovered something unusual deep inside Ragefire Chasm before he met his end attempting to communicate with the troggs. Whatever discovery Maur made never reached Thunder Bluff, and Magatha refuses to let potentially valuable secrets or relics slip away into the dark caverns beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"why does rahauro want this done","rahauro motive","why find maur satchel"},it="motive",add="1d6b392d"},{q="Why does Rahauro send an adventurer instead of Grimtotem braves?",a="Venturing into Ragefire Chasm requires slipping into the fiery underbelly of Orgrimmar, an area crawling with feral troggs and dark cultists far from Thunder Bluff's borders. Sending official Grimtotem warriors or tribal guards into the capital's depths would attract unwanted attention from the orcish authorities. Hiring an able adventurer allows Magatha to discreetly recover Maur's findings without raising suspicions among the Horde leadership.",al={"why send me","why not thunder bluff guards","why an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="0cb3748c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may find Magatha’s curiosity about creatures beneath an allied city worth watching. The Grimtotem clan’s aims often differ sharply from Cairne Bloodhoof’s open leadership.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Thrall focused on dark cultists beneath the capital while the Grimtotem pursue their own quiet goals in the same cavern."},kw={"elder rise","magatha grimtotem","maur grimtotem","ragefire chasm","rahauro","searching for the lost satchel","thunder bluff","troggs"},rel={"npc:maur-grimtotem","quest:5724","npc:rahauro","npc:magatha-grimtotem","quest:5723","zone:ragefire","subzone:elder-rise","topic:trogg"},m={start="Rahauro",["end"]="Maur Grimtotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5722},src={"Searching for the Lost Satchel"}}
E["quest:5723"] = {t="quest",n="Testing an Enemy's Strength",z="ragefire",s="Magatha Grimtotem seeks retribution after troggs slaughter her emissaries beneath Orgrimmar. Rahauro on Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise sends warriors into Ragefire Chasm to cull the troggs infesting it.",h="Magatha Grimtotem seeks retribution after troggs slaughter her emissaries beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Diplomacy Meets Savagery",b="Magatha Grimtotem sent tauren emissaries into the fiery depths beneath Orgrimmar to make peace with the troggs. The creatures slaughtered the delegates as soon as they arrived. Magatha saw the massacre as an insult to the tauren and a growing danger to the Horde. She resolved to answer it with force.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Beneath Orgrimmar",b="Rahauro carries out Magatha’s orders from Thunder Bluff. He directs warriors into Ragefire Chasm to find and kill trogg warriors and shamans. The Horde strikes deep into their underground home to thin their numbers before they can pour through their tunnels into Orgrimmar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a quest for an Orgrimmar dungeon handed out in Thunder Bluff?",a="The tauren leadership assigned the work in Thunder Bluff. Magatha Grimtotem sent diplomats into Ragefire Chasm to meet the troggs, and after they were slaughtered, her assistant Rahauro organized warriors on the Elder Rise to avenge them.",al={"why thunder bluff","quest start thunder bluff","rahauro location"},it="place"},{q="Who is Rahauro?",a="Rahauro is a tauren who coordinates expeditions into Ragefire Chasm from the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. He acts for Magatha Grimtotem, sending warriors to kill troggs and recover relics lost during earlier failed diplomatic missions.",al={"who is rahauro","rahauro npc","rahauro elder rise"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Magatha Grimtotem attempt peace with troggs?",a="Magatha Grimtotem sent the emissaries as an act of goodwill, hoping to make relations with the subterranean beings instead of shedding blood. The troggs slaughtered her delegates when they arrived, showing no willingness to parley.",al={"why peace with troggs","magatha trogg diplomacy","why negotiate with troggs"},it="conflict"},{q="What enemies need to be slain for this task?",a="You enter Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar to slay Ragefire Troggs and Ragefire Shamans. Their deaths weaken the trogg front lines and their spellcasting support.",al={"which mobs to kill","quest targets","ragefire troggs"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Can this quest be completed alongside other dungeon tasks?",a="Yes. Rahauro also offers Searching for the Lost Satchel, which sends you into the same chasm to find the remains of the failed diplomatic party. You can undertake both together.",al={"other rfc quests","lost satchel quest","ragefire chasm quests"},gp=true},{q="Where are the troggs coming from?",a="The troggs emerged from deep volcanic fissures beneath Durotar. When Rahauro speaks after the fighting, the Horde still knows little about where these cave dwellers came from or why they are digging upward into Orgrimmar now.",al={"trogg origin rfc","where do troggs come from","why are troggs under orgrimmar"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Rahauro want you to fight the troggs in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Rahauro acts on the orders of Magatha Grimtotem. Magatha initially sought to establish peaceful contact with the troggs emerging beneath Orgrimmar, but the creatures slaughtered her envoys. Refusing to tolerate such an insult and viewing the subterranean beasts as a direct peril to the entire Horde, she sent word through Rahauro to cull their numbers before they overrun the orcish capital.",al={"why kill troggs","rahauro motive","why does magatha want troggs dead"},it="motive",add="4ba56403"},{q="Who are you being sent to fight in Ragefire Chasm?",a="You are dispatched to hunt down Ragefire troggs and their shaman deep inside the volcanic cleft beneath Orgrimmar. These aggressive, primitive brutes surfaced from subterranean tunnels and violently rejected the tauren's peaceful overtures, murdering Magatha's emissaries and establishing a savage foothold directly beneath the city.",al={"ragefire chasm enemies","who are the troggs","what are we fighting"},it="target",add="5de83fed"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you strike in retribution for the diplomats killed in Ragefire Chasm, on behalf of the Elder Rise.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you help protect the heart of your capital from troggs tunneling beneath the city.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face trogg spiritual practitioners who wield primal elements in the lava tunnels, a crude mirror of your honored traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Thunder Bluff commit warriors and resources to protect Orgrimmar’s foundations."},kw={"elder rise","magatha grimtotem","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rahauro","testing an enemy's strength","thunder bluff","troggs"},rel={"npc:rahauro","quest:5722","zone:ragefire","zone:thunderbluff","zone:orgrimmar","topic:trogg","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Rahauro",level="15",faction="Horde",id=5723},src={"Testing an Enemy's Strength"}}
E["quest:5724"] = {t="quest",n="Returning the Lost Satchel",z="ragefire",s="In Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, the search for Maur Grimtotem ends with his satchel. You must carry it back to Rahauro on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",h="In Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, the search for Maur Grimtotem ends with his satchel.",sec={{t="A Grim Discovery",b="Maur Grimtotem was slain by troggs in the fiery depths of Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. Even in death, his arms clung to his personal satchel. Freeing it from his grip is the only clue to why a member of the Grimtotem clan entered the volcanic caverns beneath Thrall's capital.",sp=0},{t="Magatha's Interest",b="Rahauro receives the satchel gratefully on Elder Rise and seeks answers about why one of Magatha Grimtotem's clan died needlessly. Magatha Grimtotem herself oversaw the effort, and Rahauro gives a reward authorized by the Elder Crone. What Maur carried, or why Magatha sent him into Orgrimmar's trogg-infested fissures, is known only to Grimtotem leadership.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Maur Grimtotem located?",a="Maur Grimtotem's corpse lies deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, surrounded by hostile troggs.",al={"maur grimtotem corpse","find maur grimtotem","where is maur"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who do I turn the satchel in to?",a="Bring the Grimtotem Satchel to Rahauro on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"turn in lost satchel","where is rahauro","satchel turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why was Maur Grimtotem in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Rahauro says he does not know why Magatha's clansman had to die needlessly. Magatha Grimtotem personally ordered the recovery effort, suggesting Maur may have been acting on clan business.",al={"why was maur in rfc","maur mission","what was maur doing"},it="why_here"},{q="What is inside the Grimtotem Satchel?",a="The satchel's contents are never revealed to the courier. Maur guarded it fiercely until his death, and it is handed unopened directly to Rahauro on Magatha's behalf.",al={"what was in the bag","satchel contents"},it="item"},{q="What killed Maur Grimtotem?",a="Savage troggs ambushed and killed Maur in the tunnels of Ragefire Chasm.",al={"how did maur die","who killed maur"},it="threat"},{q="Who is behind this task?",a="Rahauro is the contact on Elder Rise, while Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem gives the directive and authorizes the reward.",al={"who sent rahauro","magatha connection"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Maur Grimtotem want his satchel returned?",a="Maur Grimtotem did not give you this mission in life—he died clutching his satchel beneath Ragefire Chasm's depths. Even as troggs overwhelmed him, his final act was guarding whatever clan secrets or valuables lay inside. Returning the satchel honors that sacrifice and fulfills the investigation Rahauro and Magatha Grimtotem set in motion to discover what befell their kin.",al={"maur grimtotem motive","why return satchel","why does maur want the satchel returned"},it="motive",add="5b8e763c"},{q="Why were you sent to recover the satchel instead of the Thunder Bluff guards?",a="Ragefire Chasm lies deep beneath the streets of Orgrimmar, far from the jurisdiction of Thunder Bluff's city braves. Entering the subterranean tunnels requires slipping past ferocious troggs and Searing Blade cultists. Rather than causing a diplomatic or military incident by marching Kalimdor forces through an allied capital's depths, Rahauro relied on capable adventurers to quietly track down their fallen clansman.",al={"why me returning lost satchel","why send adventurers ragefire satchel","why don't guards recover satchel"},it="why_me",add="2bcdc4f2"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan has an uneasy relationship with Cairne Bloodhoof's people. Any secret operation by Magatha's followers in Orgrimmar gives cause for suspicion.",["faction:Horde"]="Troggs and cultists threaten the tunnels beneath Orgrimmar. Grimtotem agents are also present beneath Thrall's fortress, raising unanswered political questions."},kw={"elder rise","grimtotem satchel","magatha","maur grimtotem","ragefire chasm","rahauro","returning the lost satchel","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:5722","npc:maur-grimtotem","npc:rahauro","zone:ragefire","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:elder-rise","topic:tauren","topic:trogg"},m={start="Maur Grimtotem",["end"]="Rahauro",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5724},src={"Returning the Lost Satchel"}}
E["quest:5725"] = {t="quest",n="The Power to Destroy...",z="ragefire",s="In the Undercity, Varimathras sends Horde adventurers into Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner wants two dark tomes held by the Searing Blade cult, hoping their power will aid her war against the Scourge and the Lich King.",h="In the Undercity, Varimathras sends Horde adventurers into Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Borrowed Arsenal",b="Thrall's orcs are hunting the Searing Blade cult beneath their capital, while the Forsaken covet the cult's occult stores. On Sylvanas Windrunner's orders, Varimathras sends operatives into Ragefire Chasm to seize two demonic grimoires: Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether. The Dark Lady believes disciplined Forsaken will can put these demonic gifts to better use than the lesser cultists.",sp=0},{t="The War for Liberation",b="Varimathras explains the tomes' purpose once they are secured. Their dark magic is meant to strengthen Sylvanas's campaign against the Scourge. By claiming every scrap of forbidden power, the Forsaken hope to break the Lich King's hold across Lordaeron and free the remaining undead from his mental enslavement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Varimathras want books from underneath Orgrimmar?",a="The Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm hold powerful demonic tomes. Lady Sylvanas believes their knowledge is wasted on cultists and wants to turn it against the Lich King.",al={"why varimathras ragefire","undercity ragefire quest reason","why steal books"},it="motive"},{q="What books are you sent to collect?",a="You are sent to collect two spellbooks from Searing Blade cultists and warlocks: Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether.",al={"what books","power to destroy books","ragefire book drops"},it="item"},{q="Where does Varimathras reside in the Undercity?",a="Varimathras resides beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"varimathras location","where is varimathras","turn in location"},it="place"},{q="How does this relate to the Forsaken's overall goals?",a="Sylvanas gathers every tool she can to wage war against the Scourge. Forbidden demonic arcana could help the Forsaken break the Lich King's dominion over the undead.",al={"forsaken motivation","why does sylvanas need spells","undercity lich king plot"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Thrall know the Forsaken are taking these books?",a="Orgrimmar's leaders are focused on purging the traitors and demons beneath their streets. Varimathras's order to retrieve the books is presented as quiet business for the Dark Lady, rather than an official joint Horde decree.",al={"does thrall know","orgrimmar undercity secret books","shadow council books orc reaction"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Searing Blade?",a="The Searing Blade is a secretive sect of the Shadow Council in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. Its members practice dark demonic magic beneath the Warchief's nose.",al={"what is searing blade","searing blade ragefire","ragefire cultists"},it="target"},{q="What are the Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether?",a="These two tomes are dark grimoires gifted by the Burning Legion to their mortal worshipers. They contain powerful demonic lore and shadow magic that the Searing Blade cultists use to advance their masters' agenda. Lady Sylvanas believes such power is wasted on lesser pawns and intends to claim the grimoires to bolster the Forsaken's struggle against the Lich King.",al={"spells of shadow book","incantations from the nether","what are the books for"},it="item",add="fcfaa53d"},{q="Why does Varimathras send you instead of the Royal Guard?",a="Varimathras has a hundred other tasks awaiting his attention, and the Searing Blade hide in caverns far away beneath Orgrimmar. Lady Sylvanas wants the cult's two spellbooks \"borrowed\" for her own ends, so Varimathras sends an ambitious adventurer to take them, promising further tasks to those who serve the Dark Lady well.",al={"why send me","why not royal guard","why doesnt varimathras go"},it="why_me",add="d6e166d9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, your journey across the Great Sea to plunder Orgrimmar's underbelly serves your alliance with the Horde and the Dark Lady's ambition to destroy the Scourge.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, retrieving Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether means wresting dangerous Legion arcana from reckless cultists.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Orgrimmar's foundations by clearing the Searing Blade, while the magical spoils go to the Undercity's vaults."},kw={"incantations from the nether","lich king","ragefire chasm","searing blade","spells of shadow","sylvanas","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","zone:ragefire","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:shadow-council","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Varimathras",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5725,ri={"Incantations from the Nether","Spells of Shadow"}},src={"The Power to Destroy... (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5728"] = {t="quest",n="Hidden Enemies",z="ragefire",s="Thrall sends you against the Searing Blade beneath Orgrimmar. After tricking Neeru Fireblade into believing you are an ally, he sends you into Ragefire Chasm to assassinate the cult's top commanders.",h="Thrall sends you against the Searing Blade beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Cancer Beneath the Streets",b="Orgrimmar was built as a haven for a free Orcish race, but its foundations conceal an old demonic threat. Beneath the markets, the Cleft of Shadow opens onto the tunnels of Ragefire Chasm. In those volcanic depths, remnants of the Shadow Council called the Searing Blade gather strength. They practice dark arts and scheme to seize the young Horde from within its own capital.",sp=0},{t="Playing the Double Agent",b="A direct assault without intelligence would leave the Shadow Council's network intact. Thrall uses you to draw information from Neeru Fireblade, a warlock in the Cleft of Shadow who seems willing to cooperate. Neeru believes you share the cult's cause and gives up the names of its underground leaders: Bazzalan, a corrupt satyr, and Jergosh the Invoker, a warlock.",sp=1},{t="Decapitating the Searing Blade",b="Thrall sends you into Ragefire Chasm to kill Bazzalan and Jergosh, throwing the cultists into chaos. The killings must remain deniable, so Neeru cannot learn who carried them out. Thrall plans to keep the warlock under watch. Removing the leaders sends shock through the cult and gives the Horde's young city precious breathing room.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who orders the hit in Hidden Enemies?",a="Warchief Thrall orders the attack from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar. He trusts you with sensitive work to secure the city's underbelly.",al={"who gives hidden enemies","hidden enemies quest giver","thrall ragefire quest"},it="leader"},{q="Why doesn't Thrall just execute Neeru Fireblade?",a="Thrall keeps Neeru alive under surveillance. Knowing the traitor lets the Warchief's scouts watch the Shadow Council's communications and anticipate plots, rather than leave room for a hidden replacement.",al={"why not kill neeru","why keep neeru alive","neeru fireblade traitor"},sp=1},{q="Where are Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker located?",a="Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker are deep within Ragefire Chasm, reached through the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. Jergosh commands the cultists from a volcanic ledge, while Bazzalan lurks in a nearby elevated cavern.",al={"where is bazzalan","where is jergosh","ragefire chasm bosses"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Searing Blade?",a="The Searing Blade is a local sect aligned with the Burning Blade and Shadow Council. Its members worship demonic powers and practice fel magic beneath Orgrimmar, seeking to overthrow Thrall and enslave the Horde again.",al={"what is searing blade","searing blade cult","burning blade orgrimmar"},it="threat"},{q="Why is a satyr like Bazzalan working beneath an Orc city?",a="Satyrs are ancient servants of the Burning Legion. Bazzalan works beneath the Orc city as a demonic handler and instigator, guiding the Searing Blade's mortal cultists to carry out the Legion's will under Thrall's feet.",al={"why is there a satyr in orgrimmar","bazzalan lore","satyr in ragefire"},it="origin"},{q="How does this quest fit into the broader Ragefire Chasm run?",a="Hidden Enemies brings Thrall's infiltration chain to its climax. It joins other Ragefire Chasm assignments that target the dungeon's chief humanoid foes in one coordinated strike.",al={"is hidden enemies ragefire","rfc quest line","hidden enemies chain"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thrall want this done?",a="The Shadow Council seeks to seize Orgrimmar and tear the Horde from Thrall's grasp. Having learned from Neeru Fireblade that the Searing Blade operates right beneath the city's streets, Thrall recognizes their leaders as an imminent danger. Striking down Bazzalan and Jergosh deals an immediate blow to the cult's underground operations and throws their plotting into disarray before they can strike Orgrimmar from below.",al={"why does thrall want bazzalan dead","thrall motive hidden enemies","why kill searing blade leaders"},it="motive",add="53ca461d"},{q="Who are you being sent to kill?",a="You are sent to eliminate Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker, the leaders of the Searing Blade cult nested deep within Ragefire Chasm. Bazzalan is a satyr commanding dark forces from the shadows, while Jergosh is a powerful warlock directing cult rituals. Both answer to Neeru Fireblade and serve as the cult's operational backbone in the caverns under Orgrimmar.",al={"who are the targets","who to kill hidden enemies","bazzalan and jergosh"},it="target",add="0041999b"},{q="Why does Thrall send you instead of the city guards?",a="Sending an army of Orgrimmar guards into the chasm would expose the warchief's awareness of the conspiracy and immediately blow your cover. Because you successfully infiltrated the Burning Blade and earned Neeru Fireblade's trust, you can slip down into Ragefire Chasm quietly. Thrall needs the leaders eliminated without Neeru discovering that his supposed recruit was the assassin, preserving your identity for future intelligence.",al={"why send me","why not use orgrimmar guards","why not send kor'kron"},it="why_me",add="1b8ff306"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face demonic corruption in the heart of Durotar, threatening all the new Horde fought to establish. Cleansing Ragefire Chasm helps preserve its hard-won freedom.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc seeking redemption from the blood-haze, you face the Shadow Council's remnants beneath Orgrimmar. Their destruction is a matter of cultural survival and honor.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know Thrall tolerates dark arts in the Horde's defense. Jergosh and the Searing Blade have instead sworn themselves to demonic masters, betraying the Horde."},kw={"bazzalan","cleft of shadow","hidden enemies","jergosh the invoker","neeru fireblade","ragefire chasm","searing blade","shadow council","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","quest:5726","zone:ragefire","quest:829","npc:bazzalan","npc:jergosh-the-invoker","topic:shadow-council","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},m={start="Thrall",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5728},src={"Hidden Enemies (3)"}}
E["quest:5761"] = {t="quest",n="Slaying the Beast",z="ragefire",s="In Orgrimmar’s Cleft of Shadow, Neeru Fireblade sends Horde adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to hunt Taragaman the Hungerer. He claims Warchief Thrall ordered the hunt and demands the towering felguard’s heart as proof the demonic cult has fallen.",h="In Orgrimmar’s Cleft of Shadow, Neeru Fireblade sends Horde adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to hunt Taragaman...",sec={{t="A Threat Beneath the City",b="Ragefire Chasm lies beneath Orgrimmar’s red earthen streets, a fiery fissure filled with troggs, beasts, and covert Searing Blade agents. In the Cleft of Shadow above, Neeru Fireblade presents himself as a loyal servant carrying out Thrall’s order to cleanse this demonic rot. He points to Taragaman the Hungerer, a massive felguard in the cavern’s heart, and names him as the mastermind behind the cult below the city.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Deception",b="Returning Taragaman’s heart to Neeru Fireblade brings high praise and promises that Thrall will be appeased. Taragaman is only an expendable brute, not the cult’s true leader. By sending Horde heroes after the demon, Neeru gives Thrall a visible victory to quiet suspicion while shielding the Searing Blade’s real leadership and deeper operations beneath Orgrimmar from closer scrutiny.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Taragaman the Hungerer?",a="Taragaman the Hungerer is a powerful felguard on a rocky platform in the heart of Ragefire Chasm. Neeru Fireblade names him as the leader of the Searing Blade cultists beneath Orgrimmar.",al={"who is taragaman","what is taragaman","taragaman lore"},it="target"},{q="Who gives the quest Slaying the Beast?",a="Neeru Fireblade gives the assignment from his tent in the Cleft of Shadow, Orgrimmar’s cavernous warlock quarter.",al={"quest giver slaying the beast","who gives this quest","neeru fireblade quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Neeru want Taragaman's heart?",a="Neeru says Taragaman’s heart will prove to Warchief Thrall that the demonic threat beneath Orgrimmar has been destroyed.",al={"why get the heart","taragaman heart purpose","why does neeru want the heart"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Is Taragaman actually the leader of the Searing Blade?",a="Neeru Fireblade names Taragaman as their leader. Taragaman is a formidable felguard among the Searing Blade cultists in Ragefire Chasm’s heart.",al={"is taragaman the real leader","who leads searing blade","taragaman leader"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Where is Taragaman located?",a="Taragaman the Hungerer is on a rock platform surrounded by lava in Ragefire Chasm’s middle reaches, among Searing Blade cultists.",al={"taragaman location","where is the beast","where to find taragaman"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does this quest connect to Hidden Enemies?",a="In the Hidden Enemies storyline, Thrall investigates the Shadow Council’s infiltration of Orgrimmar and watches Neeru Fireblade closely. Neeru offers this hunt to show Thrall visible results against the Searing Blade.",al={"connection to hidden enemies","hidden enemies questline","thrall and neeru"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Why does Neeru Fireblade want Taragaman slain?",a="Neeru claims he is serving Warchief Thrall by rooting out the demonic corruption festering beneath Orgrimmar. By pointing you toward Taragaman the Hungerer and claiming the brute is the leader of the Searing Blade, Neeru provides Thrall with a prominent scapegoat. Slaying the demon offers the Warchief a visible victory while drawing suspicion far away from Neeru's own dark intrigues.",al={"why does neeru want this done","neeru fireblade motive","slaying the beast reason"},sp=1,it="motive",add="dcb60e0c"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock working from the Cleft of Shadow alongside Neeru, you see the political tightrope of practicing fel magic under Thrall’s watchful gaze.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face an immediate threat to Orgrimmar’s safety when a demonic presence festers beneath the capital.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc striving to escape the legacy of the demon blood curse, you can find the presence of a felguard and demon cult beneath Thrall’s throne an intolerable disgrace."},kw={"cleft of shadow","felguard","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","slaying the beast","taragaman"},rel={"npc:taragaman-the-hungerer","quest:829","zone:ragefire","quest:5726","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},m={start="Neeru Fireblade",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5761,ri={"Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart"}},src={"Slaying the Beast (quest)"}}
E["zone:ragefire"] = {t="dungeon",n="Ragefire Chasm",z="ragefire",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Ragefire Chasm's volcanic tunnels shelter troggs and a demonic cult. The Searing Blade plots against the young Horde from caverns below the Cleft of Shadow, threatening the capital above.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Ragefire Chasm's volcanic tunnels shelter troggs and a demonic cult.",sec={{t="Subterranean Peril",b="Ragefire troggs erupt from deep beneath Orgrimmar into a maze of volcanic corridors and lava pits. As orcish builders raise their new home above, the troggs grow aggressive. Magatha Grimtotem sends Maur Grimtotem to open talks on Thunder Bluff's behalf, but the troggs slaughter the envoy. They yield only to force.",sp=0},{t="The Searing Blade",b="A demonic cult called the Searing Blade is more dangerous than the troggs. Loyal to the Shadow Council, the fanatics plot the young Horde's ruin from caverns beside streams of magma. The warlock Jergosh the Invoker, the cunning satyr Bazzalan, and the vicious felguard Taragaman the Hungerer lead them. Taragaman presides over an altar in the lava lake.",sp=0},{t="The Warchief's Game",b="Neeru Fireblade appears to be a warlock trainer beside the chasm's entrance in the Cleft of Shadow. In secret, he leads the local Burning Blade. Neeru sends Horde adventurers into the depths as loyalty tests, hoping to cull weak cultists and kill Thrall's supporters. Thrall knows of Neeru's deception. The Warchief uses these forays to eliminate dangerous cult leaders such as Jergosh and Bazzalan, while keeping Neeru in place to watch the Shadow Council's broader schemes.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.2","q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to Ragefire Chasm?",a="The entrance lies inside Orgrimmar, in the underground district called the Cleft of Shadow. It is near the tent of Neeru Fireblade, the warlock trainer.",al={"rfc location","where is rfc","ragefire entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are troggs under Orgrimmar?",a="Ragefire troggs tunneled upward from underground recesses beneath Durotar. Diplomacy failed to quell their sudden presence beneath the capital, which is seen as a severe danger.",al={"ragefire troggs origin","why are there troggs here","orgrimmar troggs"},it="threat"},{q="Who leads the cultists inside the chasm?",a="The Searing Blade is led by Jergosh the Invoker, a warlock, and Bazzalan, a satyr. Taragaman the Hungerer, a summoned felguard, supports them.",al={"rfc bosses","searing blade leaders","who rules ragefire"},it="threat"},{q="What does killing Bazzalan and Jergosh accomplish for the story?",a="Killing Bazzalan and Jergosh breaks the Searing Blade's active leadership beneath Orgrimmar. Their deaths show the Horde's resilience and let Thrall thwart a demon-worshiping cell beneath his throne.",al={"bazzalan lore meaning","why kill bazzalan","hidden enemies outcome"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Can Alliance adventurers enter Ragefire Chasm?",a="Any adventurer can physically enter through the portal, but an Alliance adventurer must evade high-level Horde guards and hostile defenders throughout Orgrimmar to reach the Cleft of Shadow.",al={"can alliance do rfc","alliance in ragefire"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Thrall simply execute Neeru Fireblade?",a="Thrall tolerates those who practice dark magic in the Cleft of Shadow, keeping them close and under his watch rather than driving them out of sight.",al={"thrall neeru fireblade","why let neeru live"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What is Ragefire Chasm?",a="Ragefire Chasm is a subterranean network of fiery volcanic caverns running directly beneath the orc capital city of Orgrimmar. While it sits just under the bustling streets above, its molten depths harbor vicious troggs and a hidden cabal of Searing Blade cultists plotting against the Horde.",al={"what is ragefire chasm","about ragefire chasm","rfc lore"},it="place",add="f4fa764c"},{q="Why is there a cave under Orgrimmar?",a="The caverns naturally formed as a volcanic network within the rocky earth beneath Durotar. When the orcs chose this defensible canyon to construct Orgrimmar, the fiery chasm already lay beneath the ground, hollowed out by ancient subterranean magma flows.",al={"why cave under orgrimmar","how did ragefire chasm form","caves beneath orgrimmar"},it="place",add="947efccf",nx={9}},{q="Did the orcs dig it out?",a="No. The orcs did not excavate Ragefire Chasm. It was already a natural labyrinth of molten stone and lava vents long before Thrall led his people to settle in Durotar and raise the walls of Orgrimmar above it.",al={"did orcs dig rfc","did the horde dig ragefire chasm"},it="origin",add="9252a3ac"},{q="Why did Thrall send me down here?",a="Thrall uncovered whispers of cultist activity festering right beneath his city. Rather than launching an overt military raid that would alert the traitors, he dispatched promising adventurers into the depths to investigate the threat and eliminate the Searing Blade's shadowy leaders.",al={"why thrall sent me rfc","thrall ragefire quest reason","why am i in ragefire chasm"},it="purpose",add="b0dedca2"},{q="Who is Thrall?",a="Thrall is the Warchief of the Horde and founder of the nation of Durotar. Born Go'el to Chieftain Durotan of the Frostwolf clan, he escaped human servitude and gladiator pits to unite the shattered orc clans, reviving their forgotten shamanic heritage and forging a new, honorable Horde.",al={"who is warchief thrall","thrall lore","who is thrall"},it="in_charge",add="0d5305cc",nx={12,13}},{q="How did he become Warchief?",a="Thrall fought alongside Orgrim Doomhammer to liberate imprisoned orcs from Alliance internment camps after the Second War. When Doomhammer fell in battle, he bequeathed his legendary black armor and warhammer to Thrall, naming him the new Warchief to lead their people to Kalimdor.",al={"how thrall became warchief","thrall leadership origin","how did thrall get doomhammer"},it="history",add="09eb01d5"},{q="Is Thrall a shaman?",a="Yes. Guided by the spirits and the ancient hermit Drek'Thar of the Frostwolf clan, Thrall became the first new orc shaman in a generation, rejecting the corrupting demonic fel magic that had once enslaved his race in favor of harmony with the elements.",al={"is thrall shaman","thrall class","can thrall use magic"},it="identity",add="c23e3fbc"},{q="What are the Hidden Enemies Thrall is talking about?",a="The Hidden Enemies are demonic cultists and sympathizers who dwell secretly within Durotar, plotting to overthrow Thrall's fledgling society. Operating from shadows and hidden tunnels, they serve dark powers from the orcs' past and actively undermine the Horde's peace from within.",al={"hidden enemies thrall","who are hidden enemies","what are hidden enemies"},it="threat",add="833fd6a3"},{q="Why are there demons under Orgrimmar?",a="The cultists of the Searing Blade brought demons like Taragaman the Hungerer into the depths to anchor their dark rituals. Lurking beneath the Cleft of Shadow, they use demonic power to lure unwary citizens and test initiates who wish to serve the Burning Legion.",al={"demons in ragefire chasm","why demons under orgrimmar","taragaman in rfc"},it="threat",add="606e7173"},{q="What is the Shadow Council?",a="The Shadow Council was a secretive cabal of warlocks originally formed on Draenor by Gul'dan to manipulate the orc clans and bind them to the Burning Legion. Though shattered during the First and Second Wars, lingering sects like the Burning Blade continue working toward their demonic masters' goals.",al={"shadow council lore","whats the shadow council","shadow council history"},it="history",add="0ca922e2"},{q="What are the Ragefire troggs?",a="The Ragefire troggs are a violent, subterranean clan of primitive troggs infesting the upper reaches of the chasm. Barbaric and aggressive, they burst into the caverns from subterranean fissures, immediately attacking anyone who enters their territory.",al={"ragefire troggs","what are the troggs in rfc","rfc troggs"},it="threat",add="be4be4e7"},{q="Why me, I'm not exactly a hero yet?",a="Thrall cannot deploy his elite Kor'kron guards without alarming the conspirators and driving them deeper underground. By employing eager new adventurers, he mounts a quiet, deniable strike that eliminates the cult's immediate lieutenants while keeping his own counter-investigations discreet.",al={"why send me rfc","why adventurer for ragefire","why me ragefire"},it="why_me",add="608f7b0a"},{q="What happens after I kill the warlock and the satyr?",a="Once Jergosh the Invoker and Bazzalan fall, their plans inside the chasm are crippled. You report your triumph back to Thrall, who confirms the existence of a larger web of betrayal that reaches beyond the caverns into the surface world.",al={"after killing bazzalan jergosh","slay jergosh next step","what to do after rfc"},sp=1,it="next_step",add="cbc9ae06",nx={20}},{q="Does this lead back to Thrall?",a="Yes. Thrall expects you to report directly to his throne room in the Valley of Wisdom. Slaying the cult's field masters proves your loyalty and informs the Warchief of the true scope of the subversion brewing right under his feet.",al={"does rfc lead back to thrall","return to thrall after rfc","report to thrall"},sp=1,it="next_step",add="e02585d8"},{q="How did I end up in Ragefire Chasm?",a="You descended through the shadowy tunnels beneath Orgrimmar into the Cleft of Shadow, where the city's outcasts and darker practitioners gather. Beside the tent of the warlock Neeru Fireblade lies the cleft's deepest threshold: a smoking archway that plunges straight into the volcanic underbelly of Durotar. Whether directed here by Warchief Thrall to hunt down hidden traitors, sent by tauren emissaries from Thunder Bluff, or steered below by dark whisperers testing your mettle, you walked through that gateway into the subterranean magma tunnels.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to ragefire chasm","why am i in these caverns"},it="arrival",add="02870934"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Ragefire Chasm?",a="You are here to purge a festering rot threatening the heart of the Horde. In these volcanic caverns, feral troggs have clawed up from the depths, violently rejecting peace and slaughtering emissaries. Worse still, the Searing Blade—a covert splinter of the demonic Shadow Council—plots Orgrimmar's ruin from the dark. Your duty is to cut through the troggs, confront the hulking felguard Taragaman the Hungerer, and eliminate the cult's mortal commanders, Jergosh the Invoker and the satyr Bazzalan, shattering their subterranean network before it overruns the city above.",al={"what am i doing here","what is my goal in ragefire","why was i sent down here"},it="purpose",add="9382a7ef"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, cleansing the chasm beneath Orgrimmar is a trial for young champions to prove their strength and protect the capital.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can see the dark magic of the Searing Blade firsthand in the rites and demonic tomes used by Jergosh the Invoker and Bazzalan.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, Maur Grimtotem's death at the hands of the Ragefire troggs makes hunting the beasts a matter of honor and retribution for Thunder Bluff."},kw={"bazzalan","chasm","cleft of shadow","jergosh","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire","rfc","searing blade","taragaman"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","npc:taragaman-the-hungerer","npc:jergosh-the-invoker","npc:bazzalan","quest:5726","npc:magatha-grimtotem"},m={levels="13-18"},src={"Ragefire Chasm (Classic)","Ragefire Chasm"}}
